**Definition 2.2 (interval coefficients and labelled operations).** For a
prescribed original control and $0\leq s\leq t\leq T$, use the credited
charge

$$
\Lambda[s,t]=\int_s^t
\left(\frac{(k')_+}{k}+\frac{(-k')_+}{c-k}\right)du,
\qquad
\lambda=\frac{(k')_+}{k}+\frac{(-k')_+}{c-k}
\quad\hbox{a.e.}
\tag{QC.7}
$$

The phase equalities $H_0=H_4=:H_+$ and $H_1=H_3=:H_-$ follow directly
from (QC.2); $H_2=0$. Define

$$
\begin{aligned}
a_+(t,s)&=e^{-\Lambda[s,t]/2}
       \sqrt{\frac{k(t)}{k(s)}}e^{-i(H_+(t)-H_+(s))},\\
a_-(t,s)&=e^{-\Lambda[s,t]/2}
       \sqrt{\frac{c-k(t)}{c-k(s)}}e^{-i(H_-(t)-H_-(s))},\\
a_2(t,s)&=e^{-\Lambda[s,t]/2},\\
\gamma_+&=\lambda-k'/k,
\qquad\gamma_-=\lambda+k'/(c-k),
\qquad\gamma_2=\lambda.
\end{aligned}
\tag{QC.8}
$$

The original live no-failure operator is
$K_{t,s}=\operatorname{diag}(a_+,a_-,a_2,a_-,a_+)$.
On the stopped extension it is $A_{t,s}=K_{t,s}\oplus1$.
In reduced coordinates define

$$
\widehat A_{t,s}=\operatorname{diag}(a_+,a_-,a_2,1).
\tag{QC.9}
$$

There are still five different failure names. At almost every
$\tau\in(s,t]$, their reduced Kraus densities are

$$
\begin{aligned}
L_i(\tau;s)
 &=\frac{e^{-i\theta_i}}{\sqrt2}
       \sqrt{\gamma_+(\tau)}\,a_+(\tau,s)
       |g_f\rangle\langle g_+| &&(i=0,4),\\
L_i(\tau;s)
 &=\frac{e^{-i\theta_i}}{\sqrt2}
       \sqrt{\gamma_-(\tau)}\,a_-(\tau,s)
       |g_f\rangle\langle g_-| &&(i=1,3),\\
L_2(\tau;s)
 &=\sqrt{\gamma_2(\tau)}\,a_2(\tau,s)
       |g_f\rangle\langle g_2|.
\end{aligned}
\tag{QC.10}
$$

For a Borel failure event $B\subset(s,t]$ the $i$th reduced operation is

$$
\widehat{\mathcal I}_{i}(B)(\sigma)
   =\int_B L_i(\tau;s)\sigma L_i(\tau;s)^\dagger\,d\tau.
\tag{QC.11}
$$

Its output retains $(\tau,i)$, the original failure successor and all
actual event correlations. The no-new-failure operation is
$\sigma\mapsto\widehat A_{t,s}\sigma\widehat A_{t,s}^\dagger$.
Existing live/stopped status distinguishes survival of a live specimen from
the unchanged already-stopped branch. An already-stopped branch is not
recorded as a new successful original trial; its first-failure record remains.

For the coarser finite-interval mode instrument, the corresponding reduced
Kraus operators are

$$
\widehat B_{t,s,i}=
\begin{cases}
e^{-i\theta_i}\sqrt{(1-|a_+|^2)/2}\,|g_f\rangle\langle g_+|,&i=0,4,\\
e^{-i\theta_i}\sqrt{(1-|a_-|^2)/2}\,|g_f\rangle\langle g_-|,&i=1,3,\\
\sqrt{1-|a_2|^2}\,|g_f\rangle\langle g_2|,&i=2.
\end{cases}
\tag{QC.12}
$$

The two operations within a paired mode have equal CP maps on this support;
the different outcome names, actual records and their uses are retained.
Equality of CP maps does not authorize deleting an acquired label.

